      *================================================================*
      * SQLCA — DB2 SQL Communication Area.
      *
      * Canonical source: IBM DB2 standard SQLCA copybook (the structure
      * DB2 populates after each SQL statement). Field layout follows the
      * IBM DB2 SQLCA definition; naca-rt models SQLCODE in
      * nacaLib.sqlSupport.SQLCode. Provided as a real, non-empty copybook
      * so `EXEC SQL INCLUDE SQLCA` lowers faithfully (no empty stub).
      *================================================================*
       01  SQLCA.
           10  SQLCAID        PIC X(8).
           10  SQLCABC        PIC S9(9) COMP.
           10  SQLCODE        PIC S9(9) COMP.
           10  SQLERRMC       PIC X(70).
           10  SQLERRP        PIC X(8).
           10  SQLERRD        PIC S9(9) COMP OCCURS 6.
           10  SQLWARN.
               15  SQLWARN0   PIC X.
               15  SQLWARN1   PIC X.
               15  SQLWARN2   PIC X.
               15  SQLWARN3   PIC X.
               15  SQLWARN4   PIC X.
               15  SQLWARN5   PIC X.
               15  SQLWARN6   PIC X.
               15  SQLWARN7   PIC X.
           10  SQLSTATE       PIC X(5).
